<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Writer's update feed.

  An installed copy of Writer polls this file and nothing else — the URL is
  compiled into every build as SUFeedURL and cannot be changed for an app already
  on someone's Mac. So this address is permanent, and this repo must stay PUBLIC:
  Sparkle reads it with no credentials.

  Zero <item> elements is the correct "no update available" state, not an error.
  It exists from day one so the very first build finds a valid feed rather than a
  404 the first time someone checks.

  Every future entry needs: sparkle:version (the MONOTONIC CFBundleVersion integer,
  not the marketing string — Sparkle compares that one), sparkle:shortVersionString
  (what the customer sees), an enclosure url, length in bytes, and
  sparkle:edSignature produced by bin/sign_update. An entry without a valid
  signature is refused by every installed copy, which is the point.
-->
